/math-academy-id "q-76473" :question/problem "![](images/10/103c586778cdd8181fdc8396a92472df0525fc8e1c77fde9a7c3f731dca6df07.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $OABO,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the counterclockwise direction?" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in counterclockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={C}_{1}\\cup {-{C}_{2}}\\cup {C}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{2}$ is the same path as ${C}_{2}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180280 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1409abbb-7224-58eb-8da4-c50ec502212f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342414} {:answer/id #uuid "18044e07-611f-56ee-ac44-f721c8ac319d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342450} {:answer/id #uuid "5caf092f-4769-58a7-b091-5b21981adeeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343016} {:answer/id #uuid "6826a076-9cd9-5d33-b76d-0b263e9a96dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+