se-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y+R(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+5\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89d2a9cd-860f-5996-89ba-5c6d807399c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i + j + k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177820} {:answer/id #uuid "92bed6cf-f51c-5d40-9cad-27bd23fd8555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}z^{2}i + \\frac{1}{2}x^{2}j + \\frac{1}{2}y^{2}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177821} {:answer/id #uuid "a0810d12-6ba3-58fd-bb3b-050048006770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}∇(x + y + z)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177822} {:answer/id #uuid "08a1a97b-dd4d-51a2-9817-cce63b42a512" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "zi + xj + yk" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177823} {:answer/id #uuid "45b8fefa-b254-5947-9bba-e9918a5fd738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∇(x + y + z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177824}] :answer-field/id #uuid "215217ab-57d4-55ca-a3b0-79e58a5c7e34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177819}] :question/id #uuid "f08d86dc-4f87-54db-ae1a-88ae0082bc5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-125422" :question/problem "If $\\displaystyle \\int_(C)zdx + xdy + ydz$ is equivalent to $\\displaystyle \\int_(C)F \\cdot dr$ for some piecewise smooth curve $C$, then $F(x, y, z) =$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e410ddf-84e2-5349-b99f-7b10cce11cec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}2z\\,\\text{d}x+3x\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257608} {:answer/id #uuid "8e11896f-16e5-5f59-bbed-02cfb68e20a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}3x\\,\\text{d}x-4y\\,\\text{d}y+2z\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258034} {:answer/id #uuid "9648d6f8-5662-55bf-8371-9e2f6c4805c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}-4y\\,\\text{d}x+2z\\,\\text{d}y+3x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258105} {:answer/id #uuid "be39d050-270c-5115-8d0f-7cd3ce274da8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}2\\,\\text{d}x+3\\,\\text{d}y-4\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258443} {:answer/id #uuid "e622dbb6-dbf6-50da-90af-70479db8a9bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(2z+3x-4y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e410ddf-84e2-5349-b99f-7b10cce11cec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}2z\\,\\text{d}x+3x\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257608} :answer-field/id #uuid "72c0c87b-9ed0-5e85-a70e-4bc5daad194c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259228}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "78e032bd-88b9-59d8-89ba-60a2eb488ce7" :question/math-academy-id "q-125413" :question/problem "Let $F(x,y,z)=2z\\,i+3x\\,j-4y\\,k$ and let $C$ be a path in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y+R(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}2z\\,\\text{d}x+3x\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19e81440-e84d-56cd-bb58-ec161c442251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}x\\,\\text{d}x+({y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257003} {:answer/id #uuid "5f494e8c-ad73-595a-bf25-8c0366227915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257618} {:answer/id #uuid "7b07b399-bcf2-5d7e-8ea4-1477d0096940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}({y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257873} {:answer/id #uuid "8f63ee0f-d6d5-55d0-a96d-faabbd6baae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(x-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+2\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258042} {:answer/id #uuid "fba49b65-428e-5726-bf94-6db8e1ed2b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}2\\,\\text{d}x+(x-3y)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f63ee0f-d6d5-55d0-a96d-faabbd6baae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(x-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+2\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258042} :answer-field/id #uuid "021dcd34-65cf-5872-b83c-9f85620594f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259035}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ab23b1e6-350e-57c6-bc34-78c226b2bb0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-125416" :question/problem "Let $F(x,y)=(x-3y)\\,i+2\\,j$ and let $C$ be the path defined by $r(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{2}+1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1].$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}(x-3y)\\,\\text{d}x+2\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259806 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5eb6d40c-1738-5868-a121-ed6bf6c0d399" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(2y-3x)\\,\\text{d}x-4\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257614} {:answer/id #uuid "751bbc81-29f2-5e3a-8e2b-798df9ec806c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}x\\,\\text{d}x+(3y-1)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257809} {:answer/id #uuid "88ae962d-8869-54c0-82fc-70c5851fef4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(3x-1)\\,\\text{d}x+y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257980} {:answer/id #uuid "bcb0d958-9542-52b7-aab9-12ab08f18e7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}(3y-1)\\,\\text{d}x+x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258428} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c032c0-a028-5aad-8373-05466f052f8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}4\\,\\text{d}x-(2y-3x)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7c032c0-a028-5aad-8373-05466f052f8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}4\\,\\text{d}x-(2y-3x)\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258789} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f8a6dd0-aae9-5825-810c-1c9c92473b84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259146}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0bb48414-d307-548b-9146-c35b5549d965" :question/math-academy-id "q-125417" :question/problem "Let $F(x,y)=4\\,i-(2y-3x)\\,j$ and let $C$ be the path defined by $r(t)=⟨t,\\,3t-1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1].$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}4\\,\\text{d}x-(2y-3x)\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259807 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6801901d-9ee9-5371-8b4b-d5db2b6a1458" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257701} {:answer/id #uuid "769ce3bb-7d2e-5ce5-b0b0-28c4cea5482a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∇({x}^{2}-y+2z)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257826} {:answer/id #uuid "93d7b961-74bb-5506-ae9a-49293428f19f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}∇({x}^{2}-y+2z)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258084} {:answer/id #uuid "9e78f156-7020-55eb-a260-6ad7cfa75ccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\,i-y\\,j+2z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258176} {:answer/id #uuid "dc333661-b4ae-5e54-bf73-e30af54e6c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\,i-j+2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e78f156-7020-55eb-a260-6ad7cfa75ccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\,i-y\\,j+2z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258176} :answer-field/id #uuid "25124abe-208b-52ab-a6ab-e1f14753fd21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259098}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a8a91190-7516-5928-b654-d4cd2239861a" :question/math-academy-id "q-125423" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-y\\,\\text{d}y+2z\\,\\text{d}z$ is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for some piecewise smooth curve $C,$ then $F(x,y,z)=$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y+R\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nIn our case, $P={x}^{2},Q=-y,R=2z.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}\\,i-y\\,j+2z\\,k)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-y\\,\\text{d}y+2z\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $F={x}^{2}\\,i-y\\,j+2z\\,k.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387629 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a901625-a97b-587a-a229-db393b0faa09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,j+\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387631} {:answer/id #uuid "65bb9729-0f4b-55d2-a79a-45bfa7c48b8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\,i+j+3{z}^{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387632} {:answer/id #uuid "3f3a5bf0-63dc-54c4-b414-83caa0016fee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\,i+y\\,j+{z}^{3}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387633} {:answer/id #uuid "f8d415eb-b557-5d40-a52e-e5602f1903e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∇({x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387634} {:answer/id #uuid "95642c53-04e5-595d-a5b9-d72091dfb374" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∇(2x+3{z}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f3a5bf0-63dc-54c4-b414-83caa0016fee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\,i+y\\,j+{z}^{3}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387633} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6079ffa-a6d7-5d2d-8433-f9ab6491cabd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387630}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a8e91f33-d259-5586-a72c-0ad1065dc0eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-125427" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+y\\,\\text{d}y+{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z$ is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for some piecewise smooth curve $C,$ then $F(x,y,z)=$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y+R\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nIn our case, $P={x}^{2},Q=y,R={z}^{3}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}({x}^{2}\\,i+y\\,j+{z}^{3}\\,k)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+y\\,\\text{d}y+{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $F={x}^{2}\\,i+y\\,j+{z}^{3}\\,k.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415773 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44901697-c22c-53ba-bb65-14f1081533bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12z\\,j-4\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415738} {:answer/id #uuid "49a222b7-ced0-5334-a476-927827cacddd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-z)x\\,i+2{z}^{3}\\,j-2{y}^{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415740} {:answer/id #uuid "6829492d-3f92-5206-8c0f-7015db0fd5bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-z)\\,i+6{z}^{2}\\,j-4y\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415743} {:answer/id #uuid "d7e04aa2-786d-5004-9af7-6898c9098f86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}∇(6{z}^{2}-z-2y)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415755} {:answer/id #uuid "ecda143d-5ef3-59db-8104-b35b72d657b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∇(6{z}^{2}-z-2y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6829492d-3f92-5206-8c0f-7015db0fd5bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-z)\\,i+6{z}^{2}\\,j-4y\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415743} :answer-field/id #uuid "f968e9bb-1698-556c-94c3-47e9ed5d0dfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415769}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6fc12b03-7934-57bc-b6a6-b1ef9ff5ade7" :question/math-academy-id "q-125425" :question/problem "If ${\\int }_{C}(y-z)\\,\\text{d}x+6{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z$ is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for some piecewise smooth curve $C,$ then $F(x,y,z)=$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y+R\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nIn our case, $P=y-z,Q=6{z}^{2},R=-4y.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}((y-z)\\,i+6{z}^{2}\\,j-4y\\,k)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}(y-z)\\,\\text{d}x+6{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $F=(y-z)\\,i+6{z}^{2}\\,j-4y\\,k.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415775 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3124c0f4-4c6e-55ec-9349-8032b33b382f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{y-1}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415737} {:answer/id #uuid "990826b9-b6bc-588a-80e6-36af02d8f2ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}{e}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415750} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e72ea2-4855-5111-a3dd-cd04fb8b2403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415752} {:answer/id #uuid "e80ae482-54b0-51f8-b405-74f535b48c44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}{e}^{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415759} {:answer/id #uuid "f546e017-61e1-549c-83d5-ab9a05185633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f546e017-61e1-549c-83d5-ab9a05185633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415762} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a4c61a4-7435-599c-afcf-0efe6b1cbdb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415765}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a47f5f1d-1328-52e8-8c90-bfca32946e28" :question/math-academy-id "q-125419" :question/problem "Let $F(x,y)={e}^{y}\\,i+{e}^{x}\\,j$ and let $C$ be the path defined by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,t-1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1].$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424622 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cf6d6b3-ad5e-5dc6-8ebb-24366de741cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}{e}^{y+z}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}y+{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424604} {:answer/id #uuid "90b2b589-9e4a-50b5-aade-f9285dbfd609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}2{e}^{x+y+z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424608} {:answer/id #uuid "91f4495b-123f-57a5-9de2-b6a7f1714f25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}{e}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}y+{e}^{y+z}\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424609} {:answer/id #uuid "adc05a61-f7ae-5052-9af4-0da99b3ef9f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}{e}^{2(x+y+z)}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424611} {:answer/id #uuid "ffa1700d-0795-5ad2-aa9c-b22297bf2101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}{e}^{y+z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z+{e}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z+{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cf6d6b3-ad5e-5dc6-8ebb-24366de741cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{C}{e}^{y+z}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}y+{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424604} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef1db59-b0fd-505e-b25a-7a9041ecb1ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424619}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7d70870-3ade-5c38-9cda-96260cf64575" :question/math-academy-id "q-125414" :question/problem "Let $F(x,y,z)={e}^{y+z}\\,i+{e}^{x+z}\\,j+{e}^{x+y}\\,k$ and let $C$ be a path in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y+R(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}{e}^{y+z}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}y+{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Establishing the Connection With Line Integrals of Scalar Fields"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179604 :question/id #uuid "d844a573-49a1-59c3-bec4-e409c486469d" :question/math-academy-id "e-9542" :question/problem "![](images/29/298b7b4293ff104a62107670fa2aba603b8a23e9ad042f7e270a4acf6267a2fa.png)\n\n \n\nConsider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path where the curve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r <  0$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r =         0$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r >  0$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r$ gives the total work done by a force $\\mathbf F$ in moving a particle along $C\\mathbin{:}$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r > 0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r <                     0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Since the force $\\mathbf F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/cd/cd71f379a02405bc21aecfb0bb14e9798cfbc4d7fd2c1d3a1d5221aa8d64638f.png)\n\n \nSo, $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r = 0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $\\mathbf F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/b2/b2284e7ffa962fd46333c4eca47a77473007fdd96e0813b9928f0303df8170f3.png)\n\n \nSo, $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r = 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050885 :topic/math-academy-id 3692 :topic/title "Gradient Vector Fields"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165abac8-b78d-5d8b-9797-98764bec8a25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459473} {:answer/id #uuid "9682a02a-0b80-592c-b204-2e00e64c9de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "165abac8-b78d-5d8b-9797-98764bec8a25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459473} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8082197-4ec5-5193-873e-90d47f00746b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e01fbca2-a092-5b1e-95d7-018e7d1f5edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459475} {:answer/id #uuid "5bd8e7a9-c801-5eeb-bd2b-c483bdb34b5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bd8e7a9-c801-5eeb-bd2b-c483bdb34b5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459476} :answer-field/id #uuid "422cd737-9b8c-53f2-a0cd-c12e1ad7286c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fbcc0ff-2235-56bb-aa08-904c6e3a229b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459477} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c4988b-246a-5c24-99ad-02a2f31d8f3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0c4988b-246a-5c24-99ad-02a2f31d8f3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459478} :answer-field/id #uuid "07711a4e-3e3f-5c90-b74e-ec28eded9fbf" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460605}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "58d69dfd-31b1-5851-b7cd-9ea022ec672e" :question/math-academy-id "q-125380" :question/problem "![](images/14/145b9dcc1e52dec65d64245afa89fba77e0d0cda5a919b52009e2397f3f03e16.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/20/20121d30445c9e756f1c2c024713bc6cd6f0464cfcfc24df68bc30c766c4988e.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/0f/0ff98536c275458d68deabda91f56bf63e7c8f59f5ea79c68292332d8cd58d4f.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47df525a-0d27-5474-842e-e797864d924f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459479} {:answer/id #uuid "0f4b12aa-dfc8-5cf6-bb46-fa30cda83363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47df525a-0d27-5474-842e-e797864d924f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459479} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ebe448c-6d78-52eb-b87a-c0f6378a526d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b3a5163-4335-5da1-a308-4afc6fa83343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459481} {:answer/id #uuid "2865bf65-f4fa-5527-9338-dac5b94be08d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2865bf65-f4fa-5527-9338-dac5b94be08d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459482} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6785c8-4fa8-5419-98ef-b6ca891fd2fe" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a7f457e-5e87-5921-9c97-354280faa2c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459483} {:answer/id #uuid "58d82791-fb0b-511f-a411-3a2ed07c51ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58d82791-fb0b-511f-a411-3a2ed07c51ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459484} :answer-field/id #uuid "5480c90b-6e84-5672-a102-83d8323aaae1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460608}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26c0cce0-6deb-59c6-a9c4-06e4698080d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-125381" :question/problem "![](images/50/501a3512fb4b8a1898c6dfb8816d587de4a0cd585991d9c92d2bb35d83a2853d.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semicircle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/4c/4c11b38f9e598e0cd8fc50715d2091e5bea48d188440ae8a99c84d66a6acb6b9.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/34/346007ae582fccdf4519a3d1cd50a467e19d5345238343a1311fd3348bbeb138.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259817 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25c37202-f845-5fe8-8a7a-1db1f298b82f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463464} {:answer/id #uuid "814c544b-ea3b-5e5e-85a8-e01671b5faa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25c37202-f845-5fe8-8a7a-1db1f298b82f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463464} :answer-field/id #uuid "72d39b77-fe29-5793-a0fb-0f2c0ded2a24" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464666} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66c009aa-e253-537e-b9ea-d64ce314b9a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463466} {:answer/id #uuid "ee7535b0-5862-5dfa-963f-9d8f8799fc40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee7535b0-5862-5dfa-963f-9d8f8799fc40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463467} :answer-field/id #uuid "401ef778-f261-5f37-b35b-442681079175" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe4ca179-59d3-5f0e-a769-a1d46a8dd48d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463468} {:answer/id #uuid "2ae8df09-8879-50b4-8407-98178c0cb9e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe4ca179-59d3-5f0e-a769-a1d46a8dd48d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463468} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecf5381b-d126-5634-9a8c-5944ea06f42d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464668}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ce534ad-d76e-5678-87a2-87c2bbfd4370" :question/math-academy-id "q-125500" :question/problem "![](images/8d/8dc3102ab0055d4e7dde7c79873a2c3d825fa9c803ea1ee2376a7dbe920c5535.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path where the quarter circle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/ac/ac9d8388e73a33df98ac7f04fe161ae75b27b4b01a79213c07e10d43c328d747.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/92/92e6f3ca98d7adbb34765307c0c570f55ce85f7f10cf6bef28bdb93d68a0c1cb.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cfa6683-6722-5eeb-96a9-3db5e8cf9923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463470} {:answer/id #uuid "75906f44-44f3-5c13-92f4-cc5703a4776e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cfa6683-6722-5eeb-96a9-3db5e8cf9923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463470} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8d2d0d3-81db-50eb-a9fb-a003de2f2449" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4736c250-e772-5723-98dc-f93776c74c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463472} {:answer/id #uuid "fca386ca-2828-5d6c-9232-724a2e7d32ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fca386ca-2828-5d6c-9232-724a2e7d32ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463473} :answer-field/id #uuid "63e272b7-517f-5dd8-b86c-d72d0456faf3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464670} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6a6e849-4c6b-52a5-b5eb-bf0993666973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463474} {:answer/id #uuid "7c6c0bcb-c01b-55d2-88c8-5dd7ed78b8a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6a6e849-4c6b-52a5-b5eb-b