tion/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "831cb1b1-064e-559a-8090-c5ef5904d2b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463482} {:answer/id #uuid "f119cf42-93c5-5b60-9a16-92306e80bd8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "831cb1b1-064e-559a-8090-c5ef5904d2b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463482} :answer-field/id #uuid "069a4e64-f502-58b7-afe8-73851d7f80b9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464675} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a59c28f9-7a4d-56a4-8b36-20c269b2a473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463484} {:answer/id #uuid "984ca6d5-aa97-5d84-8ae3-06c8f43e8370" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "984ca6d5-aa97-5d84-8ae3-06c8f43e8370" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463485} :answer-field/id #uuid "5285b4f0-a29a-5753-9eed-ad304e29d4c6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464676} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3250d354-20d6-54d0-97fb-d9ecc4f3e804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463486} {:answer/id #uuid "e358fd30-0443-5b9f-be75-140d1a5f4544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e358fd30-0443-5b9f-be75-140d1a5f4544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463487} :answer-field/id #uuid "c43a9049-f742-5536-9ca5-222ebee9078f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464677}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91c88aa7-9c4e-5dd7-9c30-608f94c03554" :question/math-academy-id "q-125507" :question/problem "![](images/86/866a1812bd31e0443becf35a7cc2b8df1bc84a49091a94250b60fe3533e4b172.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semiellipse is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/e4/e4232577b0687d781f702a196ae2c0060d3264c1f44a45a404a0f9da03bc0dd1.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/f7/f7cfcef37ed6a52d5bd374fae2d7a00c4d8012e9ea8dbef43165c10bcc9471be.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259844 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b9c996c-5a73-566e-bbb7-6b0823547575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463530} {:answer/id #uuid "30a2656e-d4ea-5f17-9193-df6e7c38a132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b9c996c-5a73-566e-bbb7-6b0823547575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463530} :answer-field/id #uuid "d493a8c4-7d2e-51cc-ac4a-a63d54af6e3d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464699} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4919df2b-1781-51fe-810e-b5fcd6350e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463532} {:answer/id #uuid "ae069756-d16c-5e63-af48-f69f18b462c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae069756-d16c-5e63-af48-f69f18b462c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463533} :answer-field/id #uuid "d91f3df4-dbea-5df3-a3ae-7785cf6bf841" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98296909-a163-589b-af22-9510086818fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463534} {:answer/id #uuid "5c79980a-5b04-5a68-ac76-67ef430a4d6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c79980a-5b04-5a68-ac76-67ef430a4d6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463535} :answer-field/id #uuid "592f6dad-8033-5ef7-8c01-64650a21f312" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464701}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc38a3d9-696c-596f-b353-c55f7e71f2d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-125688" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b9dd2fb4478ac443020e9cbebd64a2c9e4cdf5c7b6d5ce5cede854e0d7a3d804.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the curve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/51/51fafa71ff31592d9692348087cf0a20f6bbaa3b05e8519b4109d44207899a39.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/22/2287c33ff81973bcaef70917452c97282e0d0dd9ef06141d5beee8b53dec5836.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275259 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6861910f-6d1e-51d4-89aa-e94ccdc1daef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464408} {:answer/id #uuid "2ff3e9d8-9224-590f-a556-21e0f19a6cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6861910f-6d1e-51d4-89aa-e94ccdc1daef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464408} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2d825a4-6901-57a2-9930-5d754820d8f2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465138} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3073e19f-2806-5672-b534-cfe2db245ac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464410} {:answer/id #uuid "090dcb5c-5958-5538-8b54-75141969de9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "090dcb5c-5958-5538-8b54-75141969de9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464411} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6c59f83-3272-51a6-b5bb-233286cf4fae" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465139} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f071eee-8c41-5a00-9649-943ecfb7e8f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464412} {:answer/id #uuid "0d3e4fef-b214-5bad-bd98-71272ba97893" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f071eee-8c41-5a00-9649-943ecfb7e8f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464412} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe47fa17-0302-5990-92cb-7f28cb8bce17" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465140}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5a5b0685-d096-5d41-9e82-0f5600340c35" :question/math-academy-id "q-150018" :question/problem "![](images/67/678ab825415e107bca9554d90e2ad5a4d8cc90a5ef68d817972ef98dfc165922.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/0e/0e8d0fcf619987f49869cc6ae9eb5cb0c7acbbb23f45ce8f64626dfd1debdc63.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/b2/b2bec1f1da172b623f20d28fd0e9c5a248cf00dc621769851ca33b3b545b8592.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414784 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f0162ba-5ef3-5ddf-8884-68e373c833a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472526} {:answer/id #uuid "10f070d6-ca76-58f9-8198-433b788e83cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10f070d6-ca76-58f9-8198-433b788e83cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472527} :answer-field/id #uuid "a22ff3ac-6762-5a5a-a846-c9c1ac079ce7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473658} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a55ad75-30aa-5338-9705-0e8bb5a17796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472528} {:answer/id #uuid "2bfb901c-eb55-5a16-8c43-2a7bc4df1694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a55ad75-30aa-5338-9705-0e8bb5a17796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472528} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e84a8a1-9e86-5904-8f0e-d9bd26a8cf86" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473659} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf9bee40-6700-53ec-bc0a-8c4fbe9bdd4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472530} {:answer/id #uuid "35fcedff-2ccf-5690-9d0e-4989e5420282" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf9bee40-6700-53ec-bc0a-8c4fbe9bdd4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472530} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a2b2811-e1ba-5e92-bdc1-f1a06a417ca6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473660}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "277ca4a2-1c02-58e4-b62f-d0e1176e96df" :question/math-academy-id "q-125499" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8ffc97d4fc442503eb5b59e01f317cc7a77cf57d041e16807aa0645f962a5aeb.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the three-quarter circle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/c9/c9805268d9f4984983c3cc5e2200a0c22d804bc67076a3505ad35471693c037b.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/da/dafb4d468e7711a804a5141301a02331bb5c7900f018a8ecdb6fd382bc05b799.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414786 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "862b5ba7-c160-5733-9f50-a71ae76ca34b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472544} {:answer/id #uuid "e41ef8d6-645f-5335-a725-5df3f79d720b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "862b5ba7-c160-5733-9f50-a71ae76ca34b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472544} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6758123-2b6f-5ca7-b758-0977ff127c63" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87432ad0-fee2-5a6d-93c2-e0fdd6855b6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472546} {:answer/id #uuid "a81d96e7-72a4-5890-9d53-4c56d8d05129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a81d96e7-72a4-5890-9d53-4c56d8d05129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472547} :answer-field/id #uuid "7218a528-433c-5908-a059-6caac226974f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473668} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e9d4872-a5a3-5eb5-a69c-5fd7c7c550ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472548} {:answer/id #uuid "90531cfb-e714-59c4-8c1c-8472694477e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90531cfb-e714-59c4-8c1c-8472694477e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472549} :answer-field/id #uuid "2459159f-cb74-5c50-a417-695621954be1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473669}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7554a362-8a42-5a06-a982-68a08488fe59" :question/math-academy-id "q-125687" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1ba55883d76b7e48148febcf6203a987575e78179c2fcde1963ab9db34a37738.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the сurve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/e7/e783fb958f01da9552ef4258adf4bed1f7b083520ad9a59082b5479dc2fc7d40.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/20/20798c6992f536d4f280243746f8599bd4589bd69e253caeed65150b8a9944b7.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}]}
